l":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.6 beta2 and later\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.rc1 - Windows 11 (build 22631) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8142) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600X 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 63.92 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nSince 4.6 beta2, launching Godot in XR mode on Meta Quest 3 through Air Link causes huge flickering, appearing only in headset. Monitor preview is fine.\n\nThis only happens on Airlink, not in Steam Link and Virtual Desktop.\n\nOn my bigger project console spams `OpenXR head space location not valid (check tracking?)`, but it doesn't happen in minimal-xr-project I have attached for reproducing. Headset is correctly tracked in 3D space, though.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nLaunch game with minimal OpenXR setup (XROrigin and XRCamera)\n\nAttaching a video recorded through headset lens (**warning** heavy flickering):\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b294f86f-10c8-4ef5-89e2-87bf69b064cc\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[minimal-xr-project.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24643509/minimal-xr-project.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"patrykkalinowski","id":7796424,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3OTY0MjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7796424?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinowski","html_url":"https://github.com/patrykkalinowski","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinowski/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinowski/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinowski/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinowski/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/patrykkalinows